T72 development summary

1. Defined the actual finite-history Markov kernel with value
   `bernoulliBool (p h)` and proved its atomic joint-law formula.
2. Defined the pointwise ratio on `H × Bool` and proved the actual source
   composition-product equals the reference composition-product with that
   density. Cancellation uses only `0 < q h < 1`; no history weight is
   cancelled, so zero-mass histories remain covered.
3. Derived absolute continuity and finite KL, then used the actual
   Radon--Nikodym integral and the composition-product integral theorem to
   prove exact finite-history averaging. Source Bernoulli endpoints remain in
   the closed unit interval.
4. Converted the average to a uniform ENNReal one-step bound using the
   probability weights, then applied Mathlib's exact
   `InformationTheory.klDiv_compProd_eq_add` chain rule.
5. Packaged the actual true-decision mass as a unit-interval parameter, proved
   both pushforward laws equal the corresponding Bernoulli laws by singleton
   extensionality, applied `InformationTheory.klDiv_map_le`, and invoked the
   accepted T62 Bernoulli testing theorem.
6. No numerical experiment was run. The remaining urn, adaptive transcript,
   sequence, stopping, MSE-to-label, and PDE obligations are outside T72.
